        "title": "Finding the Number of Pivot Columns of a Matrix"
      },
      "question": {
        ":question/id": "5a793ee5-85e8-53cc-8e9b-772dc5b20e43",
        ":question/problem": "Determine the number of pivot columns of the matrix $Q,$ given by\n\n$$\nQ=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 5 & -3 & 0 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 2 & 0 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 8 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 8 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "First, we need to convert $Q$ to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 5 & -3 & 0 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 2 & 0 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 8 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 8 & 0\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 5 & -3 & 0 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 & 0 & -5 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 8 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 8 & 0\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{4} & :={R}_{4}+(-1){R}_{3} \\\\  & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 5 & -3 & 0 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 & 0 & -5 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 8 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLooking at the row echelon form, we see that $Q$ has $4$ pivots, and therefore the number of pivot columns is $4.$",
        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
